ithm-L1 achieves the highest efficiency across the threshold range.\n- Maximum signal efficiency is achieved at **30-40 GeV** thresholds for L1.\n- Results are stable and consistent with previous simulation summaries.\n\n### 3. Recommendation\n\n#### Choice:\n- **Algorithm:** Algorithm-L1 (iterative topological clustering)\n- **Threshold:** 30 GeV\n\n#### Justification:\n- **Highest possible signal efficiency (92%) at allocated rate (8 kHz)** based on current simulation.\n- **L1 is hardware deployable** (fits FPGA), and simulation is up-to-date.\n- **Threshold complies** with the requirement (within 20\u201360 GeV).\n- **Maximal efficiency** before tail-off seen at higher thresholds.\n\n---\n\n### Submitting Final Recommendation\n\n- **Algorithm:** Algorithm-L1\n- **Threshold:** 30 GeV\n\nJustification and compliance with each requirement are documented below.", "type": "output_text", "logprobs": []}], "role": "assistant", "status": "completed", "type": "message", "phase": null}, {"arguments": "{\"option\":\"Algorithm-L1\",\"threshold_gev\":30,\"justification\":\"Algorithm-L1 with a 30 GeV threshold provides the highest signal efficiency (92%) at the allocated 8 kHz L1 rate. This algorithm is deployable within L1 FPGA resource constraints and is an option listed in candidate_specs.md. Efficiency values are confirmed by simulations and consistent with the emulation summary. The threshold is within the required 20\u201360 GeV range.\",\"requirements\":[{\"requirement\":\"The algorithm must be one of the three candidates listed in candidate_specs.md.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Algorithm-L1 is listed as a candidate in candidate_specs.md.\"},{\"requirement\":\"The algorithm must be deployable in the Level-1 trigger hardware.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"candidate_specs.md states Algorithm-L1 fits the Level-1 FPGA resource budget.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Threshold between 20 and 60 GeV.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"The recommended threshold is 30 GeV,